    "updated_at": "2017-03-21T18:05:47Z",
    "body": "@annevk I'm not sure I understand what you mean. This text is trying to specify a range of values on the interval `[dirtyX,dirtyX+dirtyWidth)` (and conversely for Y). It's still true for `long` as it was for `double`, no?\r\n\r\nRegarding the note, I thought about making it one. I wasn't 100% convinced that this was just a statement. Specially because of potential color transformations, etc. But I'm up for it if you think it's a logical conclusion.",
